  ('goa', 'January', 1, 19, 32, 'Low (Dry)', 'Cool sunny days, clear skies and calm seas ideal for beach tourism', 95, 'High', 88, 'Peak New Year hangover crowds and the height of winter tourist season', 1800, 3500, 5000, 9000, 12000, 25000, 900, 1200, 'High', 'Moderate', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Extremely crowded beaches and nightlife strips; book accommodation weeks in advance and watch belongings closely in tourist zones.', 'Goa in January experiences cool sunny days, clear skies and calm seas ideal for beach tourism with temperatures ranging between 19°C and 32°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 95/100 and average hotel occupancy of 88%. Peak New Year hangover crowds and the height of winter tourist season. Budget stays average ₹1800–₹3500 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹5000–₹9000, and luxury resorts ₹12000–₹25000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹900 and local commute of roughly ₹1200 per day. Baga Beach is open, very crowded with high crowd levels, while Fort Aguada remains open, steady visitor flow. Extremely crowded beaches and nightlife strips; book accommodation weeks in advance and watch belongings closely in tourist zones. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
  ('goa', 'February', 2, 20, 33, 'Low (Dry)', 'Warm, dry, festive atmosphere with Goa Carnival celebrations', 88, 'High', 80, 'Goa Carnival parades draw large crowds across the state', 1600, 3200, 4500, 8000, 10000, 22000, 850, 1100, 'High', 'Moderate', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Carnival crowds mean higher noise and traffic; sun exposure remains strong through midday.', 'Goa in February experiences warm, dry, festive atmosphere with Goa Carnival celebrations with temperatures ranging between 20°C and 33°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 88/100 and average hotel occupancy of 80%. Goa Carnival parades draw large crowds across the state. Budget stays average ₹1600–₹3200 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹4500–₹8000, and luxury resorts ₹10000–₹22000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹850 and local commute of roughly ₹1100 per day. Anjuna Flea Market is open, festive with high crowd levels, while Chapora Fort remains open, moderate footfall. Carnival crowds mean higher noise and traffic; sun exposure remains strong through midday. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
  ('goa', 'March', 3, 23, 33, 'Low (Dry)', 'Rising heat with dry, breezy coastal conditions and Shigmo festival colour', 60, 'Moderate', 60, 'Shigmo spring festival and start of the shoulder season', 1200, 2200, 3500, 6500, 8000, 16000, 700, 900, 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Moderate', 'Humidity begins climbing; beaches remain pleasant in early morning and evening hours.', 'Goa in March experiences rising heat with dry, breezy coastal conditions and Shigmo festival colour with temperatures ranging between 23°C and 33°C. Tourism density is at a moderate, comfortable level with a crowd index of 60/100 and average hotel occupancy of 60%. Shigmo spring festival and start of the shoulder season. Budget stays average ₹1200–₹2200 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹3500–₹6500, and luxury resorts ₹8000–₹16000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹700 and local commute of roughly ₹900 per day. Dudhsagar Falls is open, good flow with moderate crowd levels, while Basilica of Bom Jesus remains open, comfortable crowds. Humidity begins climbing; beaches remain pleasant in early morning and evening hours. This makes the period a balanced window suited to families and value-conscious travelers.'),
  ('goa', 'April', 4, 26, 35, 'Low (Dry, humid)', 'Building pre-summer heat with high humidity and fewer tourists', 42, 'Moderate', 45, 'Summer heat sets in, marking the start of the low season', 900, 1800, 2800, 5000, 6500, 13000, 650, 800, 'Moderate', 'High', 'Low', 'Low', 'Midday sun is intense; hydrate frequently and limit beach activity to mornings and evenings.', 'Goa in April experiences building pre-summer heat with high humidity and fewer tourists with temperatures ranging between 26°C and 35°C. Tourism density is at a moderate, comfortable level with a crowd index of 42/100 and average hotel occupancy of 45%. Summer heat sets in, marking the start of the low season. Budget stays average ₹900–₹1800 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2800–₹5000, and luxury resorts ₹6500–₹13000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹650 and local commute of roughly ₹800 per day. Palolem Beach is open, quieter with low crowd levels, while Old Goa Churches remains open, easy access. Midday sun is intense; hydrate frequently and limit beach activity to mornings and evenings. This makes the period a balanced window suited to value-conscious travelers.'),
  ('goa', 'May', 5, 27, 34, 'Moderate (Pre-monsoon showers)', 'Humid with occasional pre-monsoon showers late in the month', 28, 'Low', 35, 'Pre-monsoon lull brings steep off-season discounts', 700, 1400, 2200, 4200, 5500, 11000, 600, 700, 'Moderate', 'High', 'Low', 'Low', 'Humidity and heat peak before the rains; carry light rain gear for sudden showers.', 'Goa in May experiences humid with occasional pre-monsoon showers late in the month with temperatures ranging between 27°C and 34°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 28/100 and average hotel occupancy of 35%. Pre-monsoon lull brings steep off-season discounts. Budget stays average ₹700–₹1400 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2200–₹4200, and luxury resorts ₹5500–₹11000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹600 and local commute of roughly ₹700 per day. Chapora Fort is open, near-empty with low crowd levels, while Anjuna Beach remains open, shacks beginning to close. Humidity and heat peak before the rains; carry light rain gear for sudden showers. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('goa', 'June', 6, 24, 31, 'High (Monsoon onset)', 'Monsoon onset with heavy showers and rough seas, Sao Joao festival', 14, 'Low', 20, 'Monsoon arrives; most beach shacks shut for the season around Sao Joao festival', 600, 1200, 1800, 3500, 4500, 9000, 550, 650, 'Low', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Low', 'Swimming is dangerous due to strong currents; heavy rainfall and lightning risk affect outdoor plans.', 'Goa in June experiences monsoon onset with heavy showers and rough seas, Sao Joao festival with temperatures ranging between 24°C and 31°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 14/100 and average hotel occupancy of 20%. Monsoon arrives; most beach shacks shut for the season around Sao Joao festival. Budget stays average ₹600–₹1200 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1800–₹3500, and luxury resorts ₹4500–₹9000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹550 and local commute of roughly ₹650 per day. Dudhsagar Falls is closed for safety with low crowd levels, while Fort Aguada remains open, subdued footfall. Swimming is dangerous due to strong currents; heavy rainfall and lightning risk affect outdoor plans. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('goa', 'July', 7, 23, 29, 'High (Monsoon)', 'Peak monsoon with continuous heavy rainfall and lush green landscapes', 10, 'Low', 18, 'Deepest monsoon month and the lowest tourist season of the year', 550, 1100, 1700, 3200, 4200, 8500, 550, 600, 'Low', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Low', 'Heaviest rainfall of the year; most beaches prohibit swimming, so plan inland waterfall or heritage visits instead.', 'Goa in July experiences peak monsoon with continuous heavy rainfall and lush green landscapes with temperatures ranging between 23°C and 29°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 10/100 and average hotel occupancy of 18%. Deepest monsoon month and the lowest tourist season of the year. Budget stays average ₹550–₹1100 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1700–₹3200, and luxury resorts ₹4200–₹8500, alongside daily meal costs near ₹550 and local commute of roughly ₹600 per day. Dudhsagar Falls is closed with low crowd levels, while Basilica of Bom Jesus remains open, near-empty. Heaviest rainfall of the year; most beaches prohibit swimming, so plan inland waterfall or heritage visits instead. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('goa', 'August', 8, 23, 29, 'High (Monsoon)', 'Continued monsoon rains with brief clear spells around local festivals', 12, 'Low', 20, 'Monsoon continues alongside Feast of St. Mary celebrations', 600, 1200, 1800, 3400, 4400, 9000, 570, 650, 'Low', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Low', 'Rains persist with occasional flooding on low-lying roads; keep travel plans flexible.', 'Goa in August experiences continued monsoon rains with brief clear spells around local festivals with temperatures ranging between 23°C and 29°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 12/100 and average hotel occupancy of 20%. Monsoon continues alongside Feast of St. Mary celebrations. Budget stays average ₹600–₹1200 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1800–₹3400, and luxury resorts ₹4400–₹9000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹570 and local commute of roughly ₹650 per day. Fort Aguada is open, quiet with low crowd levels, while Chapora Fort remains open, near-empty. Rains persist with occasional flooding on low-lying roads; keep travel plans flexible. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('goa', 'September', 9, 23, 30, 'Moderate (Tapering monsoon)', 'Monsoon tapering off with intermittent showers and rising greenery', 25, 'Low', 30, 'Monsoon eases and Ganesh Chaturthi festivities bring local visitors', 800, 1600, 2200, 4000, 5500, 11000, 620, 750, 'Moderate', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Seas remain choppy in early September; waterfalls are at their most dramatic this month.', 'Goa in September experiences monsoon tapering off with intermittent showers and rising greenery with temperatures ranging between 23°C and 30°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 25/100 and average hotel occupancy of 30%. Monsoon eases and Ganesh Chaturthi festivities bring local visitors. Budget stays average ₹800–₹1600 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2200–₹4000, and luxury resorts ₹5500–₹11000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹620 and local commute of roughly ₹750 per day. Anjuna Beach is reopening, shacks rebuilding with low crowd levels, while Dudhsagar Falls remains open, strong flow. Seas remain choppy in early September; waterfalls are at their most dramatic this month. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('goa', 'October', 10, 23, 31, 'Low (Post-monsoon)', 'Clearing skies and rebuilt beach shacks mark the return of tourist season', 55, 'Moderate', 55, 'Shacks reopen and early Diwali travel demand begins building', 1000, 2000, 3200, 6000, 7500, 15000, 750, 900, 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Moderate', 'Pleasant weather returns for sightseeing and water sports; book early as prices start rising.', 'Goa in October experiences clearing skies and rebuilt beach shacks mark the return of tourist season with temperatures ranging between 23°C and 31°C. Tourism density is at a moderate, comfortable level with a crowd index of 55/100 and average hotel occupancy of 55%. Shacks reopen and early Diwali travel demand begins building. Budget stays average ₹1000–₹2000 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹3200–₹6000, and luxury resorts ₹7500–₹15000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹750 and local commute of roughly ₹900 per day. Baga Beach is reopened, shacks rebuilt with moderate crowd levels, while Fort Aguada remains open, comfortable crowds. Pleasant weather returns for sightseeing and water sports; book early as prices start rising. This makes the period a balanced window suited to families and value-conscious travelers.'),
  ('goa', 'November', 11, 21, 32, 'Low (Dry)', 'Pleasant winter warmth with clear skies, marking the ramp-up to peak season', 78, 'High', 75, 'Peak season ramps up quickly with excellent weather across the state', 1500, 2800, 4200, 7500, 9500, 19000, 850, 1050, 'High', 'Moderate', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Crowds and prices rise fast; reserve stays and transport in advance for a smooth trip.', 'Goa in November experiences pleasant winter warmth with clear skies, marking the ramp-up to peak season with temperatures ranging between 21°C and 32°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 78/100 and average hotel occupancy of 75%. Peak season ramps up quickly with excellent weather across the state. Budget stays average ₹1500–₹2800 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹4200–₹7500, and luxury resorts ₹9500–₹19000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹850 and local commute of roughly ₹1050 per day. Baga Beach is open, busy with high crowd levels, while Anjuna Flea Market remains open, lively. Crowds and prices rise fast; reserve stays and transport in advance for a smooth trip. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
  ('goa', 'December', 12, 19, 31, 'Low (Dry)', 'Cool, dry, festive winter weather at the height of the tourist calendar', 96, 'High', 90, 'Christmas and New Year peak, the highest demand period of the year', 2000, 4000, 5500, 10000, 13000, 28000, 950, 1300, 'High', 'Low', 'High', 'Low', 'Peak-season pricing and crowding are at their maximum; book flights and stays at least two months ahead.', 'Goa in December experiences cool, dry, festive winter weather at the height of the tourist calendar with temperatures ranging between 19°C and 31°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 96/100 and average hotel occupancy of 90%. Christmas and New Year peak, the highest demand period of the year. Budget stays average ₹2000–₹4000 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹5500–₹10000, and luxury resorts ₹13000–₹28000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹950 and local commute of roughly ₹1300 per day. Baga Beach is extremely crowded with high crowd levels, while Basilica of Bom Jesus remains open, packed. Peak-season pricing and crowding are at their maximum; book flights and stays at least two months ahead. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
  ('jaipur_rajasthan', 'January', 1, 8, 22, 'Low (Dry, cool)', 'Cold, crisp mornings with warm, sunny afternoons ideal for sightseeing', 85, 'High', 82, 'Jaipur Literature Festival and peak winter season drive the year''s highest demand', 700, 1400, 2200, 4500, 6500, 14000, 500, 700, 'High', 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Cold mornings require light woollens; book major fort and palace tickets online to skip long queues.', 'Jaipur in January experiences cold, crisp mornings with warm, sunny afternoons ideal for sightseeing with temperatures ranging between 8°C and 22°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 85/100 and average hotel occupancy of 82%. Jaipur Literature Festival and peak winter season drive the year''s highest demand. Budget stays average ₹700–₹1400 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2200–₹4500, and luxury resorts ₹6500–₹14000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹500 and local commute of roughly ₹700 per day. Amber Fort is open, very crowded with high crowd levels, while Hawa Mahal remains open, busy. Cold mornings require light woollens; book major fort and palace tickets online to skip long queues. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
  ('jaipur_rajasthan', 'February', 2, 11, 26, 'Low (Dry)', 'Mild, pleasant winter weather easing toward spring warmth', 78, 'High', 75, 'Continued winter tourist season with comfortable sightseeing conditions', 680, 1350, 2100, 4300, 6200, 13500, 510, 700, 'High', 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Weather remains ideal for full-day heritage tours across the walled city.', 'Jaipur in February experiences mild, pleasant winter weather easing toward spring warmth with temperatures ranging between 11°C and 26°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 78/100 and average hotel occupancy of 75%. Continued winter tourist season with comfortable sightseeing conditions. Budget stays average ₹680–₹1350 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2100–₹4300, and luxury resorts ₹6200–₹13500, alongside daily meal costs near ₹510 and local commute of roughly ₹700 per day. Amber Fort is open, busy with high crowd levels, while City Palace remains open, comfortable crowds. Weather remains ideal for full-day heritage tours across the walled city. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
