  ('jaipur_rajasthan', 'April', 4, 23, 38, 'Low (Hot, dry)', 'Sharp early-summer heat with dry, dusty winds', 32, 'Low', 35, 'Extreme heat sharply reduces tourist footfall across the city', 450, 950, 1600, 3300, 5000, 10500, 540, 720, 'Moderate', 'High', 'Low', 'Low', 'Daytime temperatures can exceed 38°C; carry water at all times and avoid midday outdoor activity.', 'Jaipur in April experiences sharp early-summer heat with dry, dusty winds with temperatures ranging between 23°C and 38°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 32/100 and average hotel occupancy of 35%. Extreme heat sharply reduces tourist footfall across the city. Budget stays average ₹450–₹950 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1600–₹3300, and luxury resorts ₹5000–₹10500, alongside daily meal costs near ₹540 and local commute of roughly ₹720 per day. Amber Fort is open, subdued footfall with low crowd levels, while Jal Mahal remains open, quiet. Daytime temperatures can exceed 38°C; carry water at all times and avoid midday outdoor activity. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('jaipur_rajasthan', 'May', 5, 27, 41, 'Low (Extreme heat)', 'Peak summer heat with scorching, dry desert-edge conditions', 20, 'Low', 25, 'Extreme heat makes this the quietest month of the year for tourism', 400, 850, 1450, 3100, 4700, 10000, 560, 750, 'Low', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Low', 'Heatstroke risk is severe; limit sightseeing to early morning hours and stay indoors midday.', 'Jaipur in May experiences peak summer heat with scorching, dry desert-edge conditions with temperatures ranging between 27°C and 41°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 20/100 and average hotel occupancy of 25%. Extreme heat makes this the quietest month of the year for tourism. Budget stays average ₹400–₹850 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1450–₹3100, and luxury resorts ₹4700–₹10000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹560 and local commute of roughly ₹750 per day. Jal Mahal is open, near-empty with low crowd levels, while Nahargarh Fort remains open, minimal footfall. Heatstroke risk is severe; limit sightseeing to early morning hours and stay indoors midday. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('jaipur_rajasthan', 'June', 6, 28, 39, 'Moderate (Pre-monsoon)', 'Building humidity with dust storms ahead of the monsoon', 28, 'Low', 32, 'Heat persists with occasional pre-monsoon dust storms', 420, 880, 1500, 3150, 4750, 10200, 560, 740, 'Low', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Low', 'Dust storms can reduce visibility suddenly; check forecasts before hilltop fort visits.', 'Jaipur in June experiences building humidity with dust storms ahead of the monsoon with temperatures ranging between 28°C and 39°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 28/100 and average hotel occupancy of 32%. Heat persists with occasional pre-monsoon dust storms. Budget stays average ₹420–₹880 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1500–₹3150, and luxury resorts ₹4750–₹10200, alongside daily meal costs near ₹560 and local commute of roughly ₹740 per day. Nahargarh Fort is open, quiet with low crowd levels, while City Palace remains open, shorter queues. Dust storms can reduce visibility suddenly; check forecasts before hilltop fort visits. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('jaipur_rajasthan', 'July', 7, 26, 33, 'High (Monsoon)', 'Monsoon showers bring welcome relief from the summer heat', 38, 'Low', 42, 'Monsoon onset improves comfort and gradually revives tourist interest', 480, 980, 1650, 3350, 5100, 10800, 530, 700, 'Moderate', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Hilltop forts offer dramatic monsoon views but paths can be slippery after rain.', 'Jaipur in July experiences monsoon showers bring welcome relief from the summer heat with temperatures ranging between 26°C and 33°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 38/100 and average hotel occupancy of 42%. Monsoon onset improves comfort and gradually revives tourist interest. Budget stays average ₹480–₹980 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1650–₹3350, and luxury resorts ₹5100–₹10800, alongside daily meal costs near ₹530 and local commute of roughly ₹700 per day. Amber Fort is open, scenic in rain with moderate crowd levels, while Nahargarh Fort remains open, misty views. Hilltop forts offer dramatic monsoon views but paths can be slippery after rain. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('jaipur_rajasthan', 'August', 8, 25, 31, 'High (Monsoon)', 'Continued monsoon rain with humid, overcast skies', 35, 'Low', 40, 'Monsoon continues, keeping crowds moderate but rising steadily', 470, 970, 1620, 3300, 5000, 10600, 530, 700, 'Moderate', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Rising lake levels make Jal Mahal especially photogenic; carry rain protection for outdoor stops.', 'Jaipur in August experiences continued monsoon rain with humid, overcast skies with temperatures ranging between 25°C and 31°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 35/100 and average hotel occupancy of 40%. Monsoon continues, keeping crowds moderate but rising steadily. Budget stays average ₹470–₹970 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1620–₹3300, and luxury resorts ₹5000–₹10600, alongside daily meal costs near ₹530 and local commute of roughly ₹700 per day. City Palace is open, comfortable crowds with moderate crowd levels, while Jal Mahal remains open, lake levels high. Rising lake levels make Jal Mahal especially photogenic; carry rain protection for outdoor stops. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
