  ('jaipur_rajasthan', 'October', 10, 19, 32, 'Low (Post-monsoon)', 'Clear, pleasant post-monsoon days with comfortable evenings', 68, 'Moderate', 65, 'Post-monsoon clarity and cooling temperatures draw rising visitor numbers', 650, 1300, 2050, 4150, 6100, 13200, 560, 740, 'High', 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Pleasant weather makes this an excellent window for elephant rides and fort exploration.', 'Jaipur in October experiences clear, pleasant post-monsoon days with comfortable evenings with temperatures ranging between 19°C and 32°C. Tourism density is at a moderate, comfortable level with a crowd index of 68/100 and average hotel occupancy of 65%. Post-monsoon clarity and cooling temperatures draw rising visitor numbers. Budget stays average ₹650–₹1300 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2050–₹4150, and luxury resorts ₹6100–₹13200, alongside daily meal costs near ₹560 and local commute of roughly ₹740 per day. Amber Fort is open, excellent visibility with high crowd levels, while Hawa Mahal remains open, comfortable crowds. Pleasant weather makes this an excellent window for elephant rides and fort exploration. This makes the period a balanced window suited to families and value-conscious travelers.'),
  ('jaipur_rajasthan', 'November', 11, 12, 27, 'Low (Dry, cool)', 'Cool, clear skies with excellent visibility for heritage sightseeing', 80, 'High', 78, 'Diwali travel surge and ideal weather push demand sharply upward', 720, 1420, 2200, 4400, 6400, 13800, 570, 750, 'High', 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Diwali week sees fireworks and festive lighting citywide; book accommodation well in advance.', 'Jaipur in November experiences cool, clear skies with excellent visibility for heritage sightseeing with temperatures ranging between 12°C and 27°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 80/100 and average hotel occupancy of 78%. Diwali travel surge and ideal weather push demand sharply upward. Budget stays average ₹720–₹1420 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2200–₹4400, and luxury resorts ₹6400–₹13800, alongside daily meal costs near ₹570 and local commute of roughly ₹750 per day. Hawa Mahal is open, busy with high crowd levels, while City Palace remains open, illuminated for Diwali. Diwali week sees fireworks and festive lighting citywide; book accommodation well in advance. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
