  ('munnar_kerala', 'December', 12, 11, 23, 'Low (Dry, cool)', 'Cold, crisp evenings signal the start of the holiday peak season', 88, 'High', 85, 'Christmas and New Year holiday rush begins building rapidly', 1200, 2400, 3300, 6200, 8200, 17500, 680, 880, 'High', 'Moderate', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Book well ahead; roads and viewpoints get congested during the final week of December.', 'Munnar in December experiences cold, crisp evenings signal the start of the holiday peak season with temperatures ranging between 11°C and 23°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 88/100 and average hotel occupancy of 85%. Christmas and New Year holiday rush begins building rapidly. Budget stays average ₹1200–₹2400 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹3300–₹6200, and luxury resorts ₹8200–₹17500, alongside daily meal costs near ₹680 and local commute of roughly ₹880 per day. Eravikulam National Park is open, busy with high crowd levels, while Tea Museum remains open, packed. Book well ahead; roads and viewpoints get congested during the final week of December. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'January', 1, 8, 22, 'Low (Dry, cool)', 'Cold, misty mornings along the ghats with clear, dry days', 80, 'High', 78, 'Peak pilgrimage season continues with Makar Sankranti river rituals', 600, 1200, 2000, 4000, 6000, 13000, 450, 600, 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Moderate', 'Cold morning fog can delay boat rides; carry warm layers for early ghat visits.', 'Varanasi in January experiences cold, misty mornings along the ghats with clear, dry days with temperatures ranging between 8°C and 22°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 80/100 and average hotel occupancy of 78%. Peak pilgrimage season continues with Makar Sankranti river rituals. Budget stays average ₹600–₹1200 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2000–₹4000, and luxury resorts ₹6000–₹13000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹450 and local commute of roughly ₹600 per day. Dashashwamedh Ghat is open, very crowded at dawn and dusk aarti with high crowd levels, while Kashi Vishwanath Temple remains open, long queues. Cold morning fog can delay boat rides; carry warm layers for early ghat visits. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'February', 2, 12, 27, 'Low (Dry)', 'Mild winter warmth easing into pleasant spring-like days', 70, 'High', 68, 'Continued pilgrimage inflow with comfortable sightseeing weather', 650, 1300, 2100, 4200, 6200, 13500, 470, 620, 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Moderate', 'Weather is ideal for walking tours; queues at major temples remain long during morning hours.', 'Varanasi in February experiences mild winter warmth easing into pleasant spring-like days with temperatures ranging between 12°C and 27°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 70/100 and average hotel occupancy of 68%. Continued pilgrimage inflow with comfortable sightseeing weather. Budget stays average ₹650–₹1300 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2100–₹4200, and luxury resorts ₹6200–₹13500, alongside daily meal costs near ₹470 and local commute of roughly ₹620 per day. Dashashwamedh Ghat is open, busy aarti crowds with high crowd levels, while Sarnath remains open, comfortable crowds. Weather is ideal for walking tours; queues at major temples remain long during morning hours. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'March', 3, 17, 33, 'Low (Warming)', 'Rising heat with dry conditions around Maha Shivratri and Holi', 68, 'Moderate', 62, 'Maha Shivratri and Holi festivities draw large pilgrim and visitor crowds', 600, 1200, 2000, 4000, 5800, 12500, 480, 620, 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Festival crowding raises pickpocket risk in dense areas; keep valuables secure near temple entrances.', 'Varanasi in March experiences rising heat with dry conditions around Maha Shivratri and Holi with temperatures ranging between 17°C and 33°C. Tourism density is at a moderate, comfortable level with a crowd index of 68/100 and average hotel occupancy of 62%. Maha Shivratri and Holi festivities draw large pilgrim and visitor crowds. Budget stays average ₹600–₹1200 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2000–₹4000, and luxury resorts ₹5800–₹12500, alongside daily meal costs near ₹480 and local commute of roughly ₹620 per day. Kashi Vishwanath Temple is open, festival crowds with high crowd levels, while Dashashwamedh Ghat remains open, very busy. Festival crowding raises pickpocket risk in dense areas; keep valuables secure near temple entrances. This makes the period a balanced window suited to families and value-conscious travelers.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'April', 4, 23, 39, 'Low (Hot, dry)', 'Sharp rise in heat with dry, dusty conditions', 32, 'Low', 38, 'Extreme heat sharply reduces tourist footfall', 450, 900, 1500, 3200, 4800, 10000, 500, 650, 'Moderate', 'High', 'Low', 'Low', 'Daytime heat can exceed 38°C; limit outdoor sightseeing to early morning and evening hours.', 'Varanasi in April experiences sharp rise in heat with dry, dusty conditions with temperatures ranging between 23°C and 39°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 32/100 and average hotel occupancy of 38%. Extreme heat sharply reduces tourist footfall. Budget stays average ₹450–₹900 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1500–₹3200, and luxury resorts ₹4800–₹10000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹500 and local commute of roughly ₹650 per day. Sarnath is open, subdued footfall with low crowd levels, while Ramnagar Fort remains open, near-empty. Daytime heat can exceed 38°C; limit outdoor sightseeing to early morning and evening hours. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'May', 5, 27, 42, 'Low (Extreme heat)', 'Peak summer heat with scorching daytime temperatures', 22, 'Low', 28, 'Extreme heat keeps this the quietest month of the year for tourism', 400, 850, 1400, 3000, 4500, 9500, 520, 650, 'Low', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Low', 'Heatstroke risk is high; avoid midday outings entirely and stay well hydrated at all times.', 'Varanasi in May experiences peak summer heat with scorching daytime temperatures with temperatures ranging between 27°C and 42°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 22/100 and average hotel occupancy of 28%. Extreme heat keeps this the quietest month of the year for tourism. Budget stays average ₹400–₹850 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1400–₹3000, and luxury resorts ₹4500–₹9500, alongside daily meal costs near ₹520 and local commute of roughly ₹650 per day. Ramnagar Fort is open, very quiet with low crowd levels, while Sarnath remains open, minimal footfall. Heatstroke risk is high; avoid midday outings entirely and stay well hydrated at all times. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'June', 6, 28, 39, 'Moderate (Pre-monsoon)', 'Building humidity with occasional pre-monsoon dust storms', 30, 'Low', 35, 'Heat persists as the city awaits monsoon relief', 420, 880, 1450, 3100, 4600, 9800, 530, 660, 'Low', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Low', 'Sudden dust storms can reduce visibility; check forecasts before ghat-side evening plans.', 'Varanasi in June experiences building humidity with occasional pre-monsoon dust storms with temperatures ranging between 28°C and 39°C. Tourism density is at a seasonal low with a crowd index of 30/100 and average hotel occupancy of 35%. Heat persists as the city awaits monsoon relief. Budget stays average ₹420–₹880 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1450–₹3100, and luxury resorts ₹4600–₹9800, alongside daily meal costs near ₹530 and local commute of roughly ₹660 per day. Dashashwamedh Ghat is open, quiet aarti with low crowd levels, while Kashi Vishwanath Temple remains open, shorter queues. Sudden dust storms can reduce visibility; check forecasts before ghat-side evening plans. This makes the period ideal for budget-conscious solo travelers and couples seeking a quieter, discounted experience.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'July', 7, 26, 33, 'High (Monsoon)', 'Monsoon rains bring relief from the heat alongside rising river levels', 50, 'Moderate', 52, 'Kanwar Yatra pilgrims arrive in large numbers despite the rains', 500, 1000, 1700, 3400, 5200, 11000, 500, 650, 'Moderate', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Rising Ganges water levels can restrict ghat access; check local advisories before boat rides.', 'Varanasi in July experiences monsoon rains bring relief from the heat alongside rising river levels with temperatures ranging between 26°C and 33°C. Tourism density is at a moderate, comfortable level with a crowd index of 50/100 and average hotel occupancy of 52%. Kanwar Yatra pilgrims arrive in large numbers despite the rains. Budget stays average ₹500–₹1000 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1700–₹3400, and luxury resorts ₹5200–₹11000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹500 and local commute of roughly ₹650 per day. Dashashwamedh Ghat is open, elevated water levels with moderate crowd levels, while Kashi Vishwanath Temple remains open, pilgrim crowds. Rising Ganges water levels can restrict ghat access; check local advisories before boat rides. This makes the period a balanced window suited to families and value-conscious travelers.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'August', 8, 26, 32, 'High (Monsoon)', 'Continued monsoon rain with humid, overcast conditions', 40, 'Moderate', 45, 'Monsoon persists, keeping general tourist crowds moderate', 480, 980, 1650, 3300, 5000, 10500, 500, 650, 'Moderate', 'High', 'Low', 'Low', 'Waterlogging is possible in low-lying lanes of the old city; wear appropriate footwear.', 'Varanasi in August experiences continued monsoon rain with humid, overcast conditions with temperatures ranging between 26°C and 32°C. Tourism density is at a moderate, comfortable level with a crowd index of 40/100 and average hotel occupancy of 45%. Monsoon persists, keeping general tourist crowds moderate. Budget stays average ₹480–₹980 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1650–₹3300, and luxury resorts ₹5000–₹10500, alongside daily meal costs near ₹500 and local commute of roughly ₹650 per day. Sarnath is open, quiet with low crowd levels, while Ramnagar Fort remains open, quiet. Waterlogging is possible in low-lying lanes of the old city; wear appropriate footwear. This makes the period a balanced window suited to value-conscious travelers.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'September', 9, 25, 32, 'Moderate (Tapering monsoon)', 'Rains easing with intermittent showers and rising festival energy', 42, 'Moderate', 45, 'Pitru Paksha rituals bring a steady flow of pilgrim visitors', 500, 1000, 1700, 3400, 5200, 11000, 500, 650, 'Moderate', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'Ritual gatherings can be dense at the ghats; plan visits slightly outside peak ceremony hours.', 'Varanasi in September experiences rains easing with intermittent showers and rising festival energy with temperatures ranging between 25°C and 32°C. Tourism density is at a moderate, comfortable level with a crowd index of 42/100 and average hotel occupancy of 45%. Pitru Paksha rituals bring a steady flow of pilgrim visitors. Budget stays average ₹500–₹1000 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹1700–₹3400, and luxury resorts ₹5200–₹11000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹500 and local commute of roughly ₹650 per day. Dashashwamedh Ghat is open, ritual crowds with moderate crowd levels, while Kashi Vishwanath Temple remains open, steady footfall. Ritual gatherings can be dense at the ghats; plan visits slightly outside peak ceremony hours. This makes the period a balanced window suited to families and value-conscious travelers.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'October', 10, 20, 31, 'Low (Post-monsoon)', 'Clear, pleasant post-monsoon days with comfortable evenings', 75, 'High', 72, 'Dev Deepawali preparations and pleasant weather draw rising crowds', 700, 1400, 2200, 4400, 6500, 14000, 520, 680, 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Moderate', 'Book river-facing accommodation early as Dev Deepawali approaches and demand climbs quickly.', 'Varanasi in October experiences clear, pleasant post-monsoon days with comfortable evenings with temperatures ranging between 20°C and 31°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 75/100 and average hotel occupancy of 72%. Dev Deepawali preparations and pleasant weather draw rising crowds. Budget stays average ₹700–₹1400 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2200–₹4400, and luxury resorts ₹6500–₹14000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹520 and local commute of roughly ₹680 per day. Dashashwamedh Ghat is open, festive decorations underway with high crowd levels, while Sarnath remains open, comfortable crowds. Book river-facing accommodation early as Dev Deepawali approaches and demand climbs quickly. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'November', 11, 13, 28, 'Low (Dry, cool)', 'Cool, clear skies during the spectacular Dev Deepawali illumination', 90, 'High', 88, 'Dev Deepawali, when the ghats are lit with a million lamps, is the year''s biggest draw', 750, 1500, 2400, 4800, 7000, 15000, 540, 700, 'High', 'Moderate', 'Moderate', 'Low', 'This is the single busiest week of the year; book accommodation and river-view spots months in advance.', 'Varanasi in November experiences cool, clear skies during the spectacular Dev Deepawali illumination with temperatures ranging between 13°C and 28°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 90/100 and average hotel occupancy of 88%. Dev Deepawali, when the ghats are lit with a million lamps, is the year''s biggest draw. Budget stays average ₹750–₹1500 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2400–₹4800, and luxury resorts ₹7000–₹15000, alongside daily meal costs near ₹540 and local commute of roughly ₹700 per day. Dashashwamedh Ghat is open, extremely crowded for Dev Deepawali with high crowd levels, while Kashi Vishwanath Temple remains open, packed. This is the single busiest week of the year; book accommodation and river-view spots months in advance. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.'),
  ('varanasi_up', 'December', 12, 9, 23, 'Low (Dry, cool)', 'Cold, crisp winter mornings with dense early fog along the river', 78, 'High', 75, 'Winter pilgrimage season and year-end travel keep demand strong', 650, 1300, 2100, 4200, 6200, 13500, 470, 620, 'High', 'High', 'Moderate', 'Moderate', 'Dense morning fog can delay sunrise boat rides; confirm timings the evening before.', 'Varanasi in December experiences cold, crisp winter mornings with dense early fog along the river with temperatures ranging between 9°C and 23°C. Tourism density is at its peak with a crowd index of 78/100 and average hotel occupancy of 75%. Winter pilgrimage season and year-end travel keep demand strong. Budget stays average ₹650–₹1300 per night, mid-range hotels run ₹2100–₹4200, and luxury resorts ₹6200–₹13500, alongside daily meal costs near ₹470 and local commute of roughly ₹620 per day. Kashi Vishwanath Temple is open, busy with high crowd levels, while Sarnath remains open, comfortable crowds. Dense morning fog can delay sunrise boat rides; confirm timings the evening before. This makes the period best suited for social travelers and groups comfortable with crowds and premium pricing.');
